- The shelf: ready made things to put on the canvas, one gesture each.
- A person opening the editor is offered objects they recognise and not the several
- hundred classes a pack declares. Those are still here, one level down, because
- laying out the inside of a page needs primitives and nothing else will do.
$bog_vmap_app_shelf $mol_view
	- Links separated by commas, stored exactly as typed. The first http(s) one is
	- the application whose objects join the shelf, the rest are lands holding
	- component sources. One value for the whole editor, so the panel offers what
	- the scene has actually loaded; one pack per frame, so a second address is
	- refused by construction.
	links? \
	pack_link \
	land_classes /$mol_tree2
	- Every class the library holds, handed in by the editor. Read inside `Apps` and
	- nowhere else: reading it fetches, and a dead address has to take down that one
	- list rather than the panel around it.
	class_list /string
	- What the pointer is carrying, BY ITS ID, and where the pointer is. One state
	- for both levels of the panel: a class row writes its class name here, a shelf
	- row the id of its item, and the two are told apart because a class name starts
	- with a dollar and an id never does.
	dragged? \
	drag_x? 0
	drag_y? 0
	- An item asked for by a plain click, which the editor answers by putting it in
	- the middle of the canvas. A press that turns into a drag never becomes a
	- click, so the two gestures do not fight.
	place? \
	- Files picked in the dialog: an event carrying a payload, not a list the panel
	- keeps, so it is answered empty.
	files? /File
	classes_showed? false
	sub <= body /$mol_view
	-
	Title $mol_view
		sub /
			\Полка
	-
	- Everything above the second level scrolls as one, or a panel taller than the
	- window pushes the page down and takes the head bar off the screen with it. The
	- scroll lays every child into the same cell, so it holds exactly ONE node and
	- the stack goes inside that one.
	Stack $mol_scroll
		sub /
			<= Stack_body $mol_view
				sub <= stack_content /$mol_view
	-
	Items $mol_list
		rows <= item_rows /
	-
	- Where an application comes from. Outside `Apps` on purpose: a mistyped address
	- must leave the field it was typed into reachable, and the list is exactly what
	- a bad address takes down.
	Source $mol_view
		sub <= source_content /$mol_view
	-
	Links $mol_string
		hint \Адрес приложения, ленды через запятую
		value? <=> links?
	-
	- What the files carry goes into the component library of the user, whose link
	- joins the field above, so from that moment on it is the library any other
	- scene would be handed.
	Import $mol_view
		sub /
			<= Import_open $mol_button_open
				hint \Файлы .view.tree модуля mol. Объявления приедут, поведение — нет
				accept \.tree
				multiple true
				files? <=> files?
			<= Import_title $mol_view
				sub /
					\Файлы модуля
	-
	- Rendered only while there is something to say, like the refusals of the field.
	Import_note $mol_view
		sub / <= import_note? \
	-
	- CRUD over the library of the user, the same store the publish button holds:
	- both write into the one library the home land points at.
	Store $bog_vmap_app_publish_store
	-
	- What was typed and not taken. A second pack is refused by construction, and a
	- person who typed one has to learn that from the screen rather than from a log.
	Note $mol_view
		sub / <= rejected_note \
	-
	- Objects of the connected application: every class it declares that is not part
	- of the framework. A deployed application is a library of components already,
	- so this needs nothing of its author.
	Apps $mol_view
		sub <= apps_content /$mol_view
	-
	Apps_head $mol_view
		sub /
			<= apps_title \
	-
	App_list $mol_list
		rows <= app_rows /
	-
	- In place of the list and not beside it: there is nothing to list, and a dead
	- address is the whole content of the section until it is fixed.
	Apps_note $mol_view
		sub / <= app_error \
	-
	- The second level, folded away by default. A check and not an expander: the
	- palette has to GROW into whatever the shelf left, and an expander would size it
	- by its content, leaving the class list no height to scroll in.
	Level $mol_check
		title \Все классы пака
		hint \Классы донорского пака целиком: примитивы, из которых верстают внутри блока
		checked? <=> classes_showed?
	-
	- The old palette, demoted. Rendered only while it is open, so a folded panel
	- does not fetch a class tree it is not showing.
	Palette $bog_vmap_app_palette
		compact true
		pack_link <= pack_link
		land_classes <= land_classes
		dragged? <=> dragged?
		drag_x? <=> drag_x?
		drag_y? <=> drag_y?
	-
	- One row per item. Pointer down and not the native drag protocol, which cannot
	- be driven by synthetic events and would hand the drop to the browser.
	Item_row* $bog_vmap_app_palette_item
		title <= item_title* \
		hint <= item_hint* \
		click? <=> item_click*? null
		drag_start? <=> item_drag*? null
